{:adr-id "2607154200"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-932 — Amusement/Recreation Facility Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 932 (Other amusement and recreation activities) -- amusement
  parks, arcades, recreational facilities not elsewhere classified. Third
  Wave 4 actor in the ISIC-90/92/93 arts/entertainment/recreation cluster
  (after isic-900 performing-arts venue, isic-931 sports facility). Fresh
  scaffold under the verified-redo discipline (ADR-2607152500), mirrored on
  isic-931's module shape."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor for amusement/recreation facility back-office
   administration. Closed five-op allowlist, all :effect :propose:
   schedule-facility-booking, coordinate-maintenance-schedule-proposal,
   coordinate-supply-request, coordinate-guest-services-logistics,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates). An op outside this set is the
   SAME failure mode as forbidden-scope content, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1) facility/booking-
   record unverified -- target must be independently :registered?/
   :verified? in the store, never trusted from the proposal's own claim;
   (2) effect-not-propose -- any :effect other than :propose is a claim to
   directly actuate outside governance; (3) scope-exclusion -- any
   proposal (any op) touching ride-safety-inspection/certification,
   operational-readiness (go/no-go), pricing/programming policy, or
   safety-authority territory, evaluated unconditionally via a lower-cased
   EN+JA substring scan of the proposal's own content, qualified so
   flag-safety-concern is exempt (it always escalates rather than
   auto-committing, so it can never collide with the scan). Escalation
   (soft): flag-safety-concern always, low confidence otherwise.
   amusementfacilityops.phase independently agrees -- flag-safety-concern
   never auto-commits at any phase."
  :module-shape
  "amusementfacilityops.store (MemStore, string-keyed facility/booking
   directory, append-only ledger), advisor (mock + real-LLM seam via
   langchain.model), governor (three HARD checks), phase (0->3 rollout),
   operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph: intake->advise->govern->decide->
   commit|hold|escalate), sim (demo driver, 5 scenarios)."}
 :consequences
 ["Registry entry corrected in place (exact-text edit of the existing"
  " {:id \"932\" ...} block, independently EDN-parse-validated before and"
  " after the edit): :repo/:business-id updated to"
  " cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-932, :maturity :implemented,"
  " :robotics stripped from :required-technologies"
  "Actor repo cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-932 scaffolded and pushed to main, public"
  "Test suite (store/governor/operation/phase) run by the building session: all green"
  "clojure -M:run (sim demo) walked all 5 scenarios without error"
  "This ADR pair landed in a follow-up step after the building session"
  " left it uncommitted to main; content reconstructed from the live"
  " actor repo source and the building session's own report"]
 :references
 ["cloud-itonami-isic-931/ (module-shape mirror, ADR-2607154100)"
